    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="0704" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9131/133: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-21T11:00:00+03:25">December 21,
                            1940—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>275. Referring to the Legation’s telegram No. 265, December 5, 2 p.m., the Prime
                    Minister and the Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs on the occasion of my
                    official calls and the Shah himself when <pb facs="0705" n="693" xml:id="pg693"
                    /> I presented my letter of credence all pointedly expressed interest in the
                    early conclusion of the trade agreement.</p>
                <p>Report<anchor n="92" xml:id="d626-f1"/> called for in Department’s 119, November
                    19, 5 p.m. will be forwarded in the next pouch, December 28, for transmission
                    via trans-Atlantic airmail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d626-f1" n="92" xml:id="d626-f1-content">
                <p>Submitted as an enclosure to despatch No. 8, December 23, 1940, from the Minister
                    in Iran; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
